# =============================================================================
# repete — Runs a test N times; every run must pass.
# =============================================================================
#
# What this teaches:
#   • `repete <N>` runs the test case N times and passes only if every run
#     passes; it does not retry until one run passes.
#   • Declared as a test modifier on `proba`
#
# Common mistakes:
#   • Treating `repete` as retry-until-pass — all N runs must pass.
#   • Confusing `repete` (test repetition modifier) with `itera` (loop iterator) or `fac`/`dum` (loop constructs).
#
# See also: fragilis
# =============================================================================

# repete — repeat test modifier
#
# GRAMMAR:
#   testModifier :← 'repete' integer
#
# EXPECTED RUNNER OUTCOME:
#   `faber test corpus/repete/repete.fab` runs the passing case twice; it passes
#   only when both executions pass.
#
# BACKEND:
#   declaration-only test modifier (whitelist: repete/repete.fab).
#

test "two passing runs" repeat 2 {
    assert true
}
